{"aligned_passages":[],"lenses":{},"neighborhood_href":"/api/v1/neighborhood?manifest=41f03ec0a8b1d30d68310120008da72a73f8c3f4cc88d65acbde651f5ad06a20&ref=sha256%3A9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5%2Fevidence%2Ffixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","record":{"command":[],"details":"The long-record reconstruction extracts the spatial inequality used in order-parameter-regularity.tex:116–150: replace the coefficient by c at one shrinking neighborhood, preserve monotonicity, choose a fixed compact strip and common L1 bound, and pass derivatives through order four evaluated along coupled paths. Minimality supplies none of this transfer; it is used in the density consumer to establish smoothness, c>0 and moment saturation. On a positive plateau the third-time-derivative identity supplies the curvature consumer. Separately, SampleJets.lean:135–143 gives the scaled inequality for the SKSupport canonical diffusion at a positive continuity time; lines 90–133 supply its two dominated-convergence limits and CoerciveMoments.lean:15–17 fixes the powers of c. Division by c^2 for c>0 produces the normalized common expression. These are source-located mathematical warrants, not extracted dependency edges, a checked cross-model transport, or formal acceptance.","id":"fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","kind":"semantic_review","source_ids":["authored_long_comparisons_20261024","support_source_sample_jets","support_source_coercive_moments","support_tex_regularity","scalar-r2-26-source-order-parameter-regularity"],"status":"not_run","subject_ids":["support.fixed_time_spatial_coercivity","support.integrated_coercivity","support.regularity","support.diffusion","support.positive_curvature","scalar.constant_curvature","scalar.smooth_positive_density"],"tool":"Authored source comparison; independent semantic acceptance not run"},"ref":"sha256:9a43c3eddb32c8ae6201629ef2e4df2d94167dc286a45dd429a8dff192df88b5/evidence/fixed_time_spatial_warrant_20261025","relati